# --- Local / machine-specific settings (may contain local paths) ---
# Per-machine, and EVERY sibling of them. The two names were pinned exactly, then
# `.bak-*` was added when the backups turned out to hold X4_NEXUS_KEY -- and the
# very next commit created `.tmp<pid>` render targets that matched neither. Two
# explicit patterns became three, and a fourth sibling was a matter of time.
#
# So the rule is now stated the other way round: ignore the file and ANY suffix of
# it, and re-include the one template that must stay tracked. A glob plus a
# negation says "everything except the example" directly, instead of depending on
# nobody ever adding a suffix. The negation is what the earlier explicit-pattern
# comment was really protecting, and it could only protect it by enumeration.
#
# The carry-over deliberately preserves X4_NEXUS_KEY into every rewrite, so each
# of these holds the key plus that machine's absolute paths. A crash between
# render and move leaves the temp behind, `git status` shows it, and `git add -A`
# would stage a private key.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json.*
!.claude/settings.local.json.example
# The path config lives at the toolkit root since 4.0 (Plan 3 lane I), its template beside it.
# Anchored: only the ROOT copy is per-machine config.
/x4-paths.env
/x4-paths.env.*
!/x4-paths.env.example
# 3.x leftovers in .claude/ (still read, deprecated) carry the key too -- and the old
# template there is no longer the template, so it is not re-included.
.claude/x4-paths.env
.claude/x4-paths.env.*
.claude/.reference-buildid

# --- Runtime backups (generated as Claude edits files) ---
.claude/backups/

# ============================================================
# NEVER COMMIT EGOSOFT GAME DATA (copyright) — these are the
# unpacked base game / DLC and packed archives. Redistributing
# them violates Egosoft's terms and will get the repo removed.
# ============================================================
reference/
# ...but a SKILL's reference/ folder is toolkit documentation, not game data. The bare rule
# above also matched .claude/skills/x4-cli-reference/reference/ and silently kept all 11
# generated help files out of every commit; the suite was green only on the machine that
# generated them (code review, 2026-09-13). Re-inclusion works because the skill's own
# directory is not excluded; test_cli_reference.py pins it.
!.claude/skills/*/reference/
# The skills' SOURCE moved to agent/skills/ (gen-agent-trees.py renders .claude/skills from it),
# and the same bare rule matched it there too. Pinned by the same COMMITTABLE test.
!agent/skills/*/reference/
# Codex and generic agents get the same skills under .agents/skills/ (Plan 2); MEASURED 2026-10-02
# the bare rule matched there too. Pinned by the same COMMITTABLE test.
!.agents/skills/*/reference/
# OpenCode gets them under .opencode/skills/ (Plan 3). MEASURED 2026-10-04 (CI run 37172347642):
# the bare rule matched there too and all 11 files were never committed. Pinned by
# test_every_generator_owned_path_is_TRACKED_and_SHIPS, which asks git ls-files per generated path.
!.opencode/skills/*/reference/
extensions/
*.cat
*.dat
*.sig
lang.dat
X4.exe

# --- Never commit saves / profile / logs ---
save/
*.xml.gz
debug.txt
content.xml
config.xml
# ...but the toolkit SHIPS a game extension, and an X4 extension without its manifest
# does not load AT ALL -- silently, with no error line anywhere. MEASURED 2026-09-01:
# `git archive HEAD mods/` listed 3 files and no content.xml, so every install from a
# release tarball would have carried a dead mod. The broad ignore above stays as
# defence for anyone who copies a profile into the tree; this exempts only our own.
!mods/**/content.xml

# --- Python (x4validate) ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Node ---
node_modules/

# --- OS noise ---
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Per-mod --update timings for gates/perf_guard.py — MACHINE-LOCAL by design
# (wall-clock differs per machine; a committed baseline would fail everywhere else)
tools/x4validate/.perf-baseline.json

# gates/mutation_probe.py crash-safety artifacts (see tools/x4validate/gates/).
# The marker means the tree MAY BE MUTATED right now; the pristine copies are how
# it recovers without depending on `finally`, which does not run on SIGKILL.
tools/x4validate/.mutation-probe-active
tools/x4validate/.mutation-probe-pristine/
tools/x4validate/.claude-md-budget-baseline.json

# hook test sandbox (scripts/test-hooks.sh)
.test-sandbox/

# Release bundles built by scripts/build-release.sh. Derived from a git ref, so
# committing one would store the same bytes twice and let a stale copy sit beside
# a moved tag.
dist/

# Nexus release packs are the USER's local artifact, not code: pasted into the Nexus
# page by hand and deleted locally once posted, every release. Tracked, each deletion
# left tracked-but-absent files that made control_bytes refuse and held the suite at
# 2 failures indefinitely. User decision 2026-09-13; enforced by
# tools/x4validate/tests/test_nexus_packs_are_never_tracked.py.
release/nexus/

# Local audit evidence contains machine paths, copied logs and game/save data.
# Keep the portable audit scripts tracked; never ship their raw output.
/audit-output/

# Codex (lane B): hooks.json carries the ABSOLUTE project root (part of Codex's trust hash),
# so deploy and the installers render it per install; the adapter's unknown-tool log is local.
/.codex/hooks.json
/.codex/x4-unknown-tools.log

# OpenCode (Plan 3 lane L): the permission deny rules name this machine's absolute roots,
# so the installers render them per install (.opencode/hooks/opencode_config.py write).
/.opencode/opencode.jsonc
/KNOWLEDGEBASE.local.md
/KNOWLEDGEBASE.pre-4.0-*.md
